---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const title = "Fallen Lineage Tier List – Best Classes Ranked";
const description = "The definitive Fallen Lineage tier list ranking all classes from S-tier to B-tier. Discover the best classes for PvP and PvE with build tips and strengths.";
const h1 = "Fallen Lineage Tier List";

const siblingLinks = [
  { title: "Classes Guide", href: "/classes", desc: "Detailed breakdown of mechanics and skill rotations." },
  { title: "Roblox Codes", href: "/codes", desc: "Redeem free spins and gems to reroll stats." },
  { title: "Official Trello", href: "/trello", desc: "Check upcoming developer balance roadmaps." }
];

const lastUpdatedDate = "November 16, 2026";
---

<Base
  title={title}
  description={description}
  h1={h1}
  siblingLinks={siblingLinks}
>
  <div style="margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
    <span class="badge badge-amber">Meta Rankings</span>
    <h1 style="margin-top: 0.75rem;">{h1}</h1>
    <div class="meta-banner">
      <span><strong>Category:</strong> PvE & Dungeon Viability</span>
      <span>&bull;</span>
      <span><strong>Updated:</strong> {lastUpdatedDate}</span>
    </div>
    <p>
      Our comprehensive <strong>Fallen Lineage tier list</strong> ranks every available character archetype based on clear speed, survival sustainability, and boss encounter efficiency in the turn-based roguelite loop.
    </p>
  </div>

  <section>
    <h2>S/A/B Tier Rankings Breakdown</h2>
    <p>
      Classes are categorized into distinct tiers reflecting overall strength across dungeon runs:
    </p>

    <div class="table-wrapper">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Tier</th>
            <th>Class Archetype</th>
            <th>Primary Strengths</th>
            <th>Role Focus</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td>
              <span class="badge badge-amber" style="font-weight: 800; font-size: 0.9rem;">S Tier</span>
            </td>
            <td><strong>Elementalist (Mage)</strong></td>
            <td>Screen-wide elemental cleave, exceptional wave clearing, freeze crowd control.</td>
            <td>AoE Magic DPS</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>
              <span class="badge badge-amber" style="font-weight: 800; font-size: 0.9rem;">S Tier</span>
            </td>
            <td><strong>Vanguard (Knight)</strong></td>
            <td>High defensive threshold, reliable armor scaling, passive turn regeneration.</td>
            <td>Physical Tank / Brawler</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>
              <span class="badge badge-green" style="font-weight: 800; font-size: 0.9rem;">A Tier</span>
            </td>
            <td><strong>Cleric / Paladin</strong></td>
            <td>Team barrier buffs, direct heals, bonus holy damage against corrupted bosses.</td>
            <td>Support / Sustain</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>
              <span class="badge badge-green" style="font-weight: 800; font-size: 0.9rem;">A Tier</span>
            </td>
            <td><strong>Shadowblade (Rogue)</strong></td>
            <td>Rapid single-target burst, bleed stacking, high evasion against boss heavy hits.</td>
            <td>Single-Target Assassin</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>
              <span class="badge" style="background-color: rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.2); color: #cbd5e1; font-weight: 800; font-size: 0.9rem;">B Tier</span>
            </td>
            <td><strong>Spellblade (Hybrid)</strong></td>
            <td>Versatile elemental infusion, flexible gear requirements, but demands high stat investment.</td>
            <td>Hybrid Specialist</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section style="margin-top: 3rem;">
    <h2>Why Each Tier is Positioned Here</h2>
    
    <div class="card" style="margin-bottom: 1.25rem;">
      <h3 style="margin-top: 0; color: var(--accent-amber-light);">S-Tier: The Meta Champions</h3>
      <p>
        S-tier archetypes represent the pinnacle of dungeon efficiency. In a turn-based system where taking hits chips away at your run longevity, S-tier classes either kill packs before mobs act (Mage) or completely mitigate incoming burst damage with active mitigation (Knight). They require minimal gear luck to complete basic runs.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="card" style="margin-bottom: 1.25rem;">
      <h3 style="margin-top: 0; color: #34d399;">A-Tier: Solid & Dependable Clearers</h3>
      <p>
        A-tier choices offer steady, reliable progression. While they may take an extra turn or two to clear multi-mob chambers, their utility (such as Paladin's healing or Rogue's single-target execution) makes them exceptionally safe choices for deep dungeon diving and cooperative runs.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
      <h3 style="margin-top: 0; color: #cbd5e1;">B-Tier: Niche & High-Investment</h3>
      <p>
        B-tier archetypes are not weak by design, but they suffer from high resource requirements early on. Without dedicated stat rolling and optimized relic synergies, their damage-to-mana ratio falls behind until mid-to-late game progression is established.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section style="margin-top: 3rem;">
    <h2>Tier List vs. Classes Guide: How to Use Both</h2>
    <p>
      We maintain a deliberate distinction between our competitive rankings and our class mechanics:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>This Tier List (`/tier-list`)</strong>: Focuses on competitive viability, meta shifts, clear speeds, and return on investment for end-game content.</li>
      <li><strong>The Classes Guide (`/classes`)</strong>: Details skill trees, level progression, active ability combinations, and lore for every class individually.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      If you want to master a specific class rotation, visit our comprehensive <a href="/classes">Classes Guide</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section style="margin-top: 3rem;">
    <h2>Recent Balance Adjustments</h2>
    <p>
      Following recent balance adjustments in the November patch, multi-hit elemental spells received scaling tweaks to prevent extreme burst variance. Tank cooldowns were also standardized to improve solo run reliability. For full changelog entries, refer to our <a href="/updates">Patch Notes</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>
